    "id": "Q002",
    "question": "What is the maximum probation period for a private sector employee?",
    "answer": "The maximum probation period is **six (6) months from the date of commencement of work**. Under Article 9 of Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021, the employer may appoint the worker under a probationary period not exceeding six months.\n\n**Source:** Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021, Article 9 (Probationary Period).\n\n*(Note: Federal Decree-Law No. 9 of 2022, Article 8 sets the same six-month maximum, but that law governs domestic workers specifically.)*",
