    "id": "Q004",
    "question": "How much notice must an employer give to end a worker's employment during probation?",
    "answer": "Under Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021, Article 9(1), the employer may terminate a worker's employment during the probationary period after notifying the worker in writing at least fourteen (14) days before the date specified for termination of service.",
