  {
    "id": "Q005",
    "question": "I'm a foreign worker on probation and want to leave the UAE altogether. What notice do I give and what are the risks?",
    "answer": "Under Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021, Article 9(4), if you are a foreign worker on probation and wish to terminate the employment contract to leave the State, you must notify the employer in writing **not less than fourteen (14) days from the date specified for the termination of the contract**.\n\nRegarding risks, the same provision states that if you wish to return to the State and obtain a new work permit within **three (3) months from the date of departure**, the new employer must pay the compensation stipulated in Clause (3) of Article 9, unless you and the original employer agree otherwise. Additionally, Article 9(6) provides that if the foreign worker leaves the State without abiding by the provisions of Article 9, **he shall not be granted a work permit to work in the State for one year from the date of leaving the State**.\n\n(Source: Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021, Article 9.)",
